m/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Tested locally, it mostly works as expected.\n\nSome feedback:\n\nThe yellow highlight is not visible on colored text:\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d9dad8cd-6542-46b8-bc03-d3df84a460e5\n\nUsing `push_bgcolor` to change the background color instead doesn't seem to work (I tried this).\n\nThere's also some strange behavior regarding highlighting: it highlights the first two lines (the engine startup lines), but doesn't highlight the first line of printed text with no formatting.\n\nScript used for testing:\n\n```gdscript\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tprint(\"Unformatted text\")\n\n\t# Using BBCode in standard `print()` will display colors in the Output panel, but not in the terminal output.\n\t# It also won't automatically reset all tags at the end of the `print()` like `print_rich()` does,\n\t# which can lead to stray formatting on following lines.\n\t# This is also the case on `master`.\n\tprint(\"[color=red]Hello[/color] world\")\n\tprint(\"[color=green]Hello world\")\n\tprint(\"Another hello world\")\n\tprint(\"\")\n\tprint(\"===\")\n\n\tprint(\"\")\n\n\tprint_rich(\"[color=red]Hello[/color] world\")\n\tprint_rich(\"[color=green]Hello world\")\n\tprint_rich(\"Another hello world\")\n\tprint_rich(\"\")\n\tprint_rich(\"===\")\n```","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/1196